    "id": "04637d835d33f887a29846a2f3c1855146151985",
    "tree_id": "6f4858c9e9d92663d392bad3a21bf488965465e8",
    "message": "fix(release): purge restored workspace bytecode in the release test job (BUG-0065 root cause) (#9624)\n\nRoot cause of the three identical release-lane failures (cohort-report\n[ASSERTION_FAILURE] 122/5, verdicts collapsed to 'unverified'): the\nrelease test job runs in the prepared-env RESTORE lane, which skips\nsetup-racket's stale-bytecode purge. Restored .zo snapshots carry mtimes\nNEWER than the fresh checkout, so Racket executes the producer's\nbytecode instead of the checked-out sources. Proven by the executed\nsuite name in the CI artifact: 'final-claim verdict cohort (c3,\nv1.00.27 w5)' — lowercase — a W5-development-era source that does not\nexist in the tagged tree (the tag's file reads uppercase '(C3, ... W5)').\n\n- release.yml test job: purge all workspace .zo/compiled before the\n  fast suite (preserving the frozen metadata-discovery fixture), so the\n  lane tests exactly what it checked out\n- test-ci-cohort-report.rkt: permanent BUG-0065 diagnostic dump — the\n  fully-guarded gate state lands in per-file output on every run\n- workflow-contract tests pin the purge step and the diagnostics\n\nLocal reproduction matched the mechanism exactly: editing the test\n(recompile) over a stale module .zo reproduced the 5 failures;\npurging fixed it (25/25).\n\nCo-authored-by: coinerd <coinerd@users.noreply.github.com>",
    "timestamp": "2026-09-08T15:25:23Z",
    "author": {
      "name": "coinerd",
      "email": "zeiler@outlook.com"
    },
    "committer": {
      "name": "GitHub",
      "email": "noreply@github.com"
    }
  },
